WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.579
"Flushing Calories with Fiber for Weight Loss"

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.800
Fiber seems so, well, boring.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.400
It's not one
of the nutrition topics

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.120
commonly placed
among cutting-edge research.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.320
By definition,
fiber is indigestible,

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.160
can't be absorbed
into the body.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.000
So, it just stays in our gut
to bulk up our stool.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.040
This is not to belittle

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.360
the importance
of bowel regularity.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.600
Constipation is a global issue.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.360
In the United States,
for example,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.280
chronic idiopathic constipation
impacts 5% of people.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.520
If even half
of the adult U.S. population

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.840
ate three more grams
of fiber a day,

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.200
a quarter cup (50-60g)
of cooked beans,

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.120
or a bowl of oatmeal,

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.960
we could relieve
enough constipation

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.640
to save billions of dollars
in medical costs annually.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.920
But it's not like we thought
fiber really did anything.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.840
In fact, you can get
the same laxative effect

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.160
with indigestible
plastic particles.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.880
Feeding people
a couple spoonfuls

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.080
of sliced polyvinyl tubing,
not recommended,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.080
ends up increasing
their stool bulk, frequency,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.960
and softening the consistency.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.560
So, for decades,
fiber was viewed

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.960
as a similarly inert,
indigestible substance.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.200
We've since moved beyond
fiber's classic function

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.960
as an anti-constipation agent

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.680
to recognizing
its other beneficial effects,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.120
including the many ways
it can facilitate weight loss.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.320
The first major review,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.400
"Dietary Fiber
and Weight Regulation,"

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.160
based on a dozen
interventional studies

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.280
where people were randomized

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.000
into higher
or lower fiber diets,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.360
found that the additional
consumption

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.960
of 14 grams of fiber a day

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.280
led to an average weight loss
of 4 pounds (1.8 kg)

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.760
over 3.8 months.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.680
That's only about
a pound (0.45 kg) a month,

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.680
but the weight loss was greater
among those with excess weight.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.760
Study participants
with overweight or obesity

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.120
lost triple the weight
compared to lean individuals.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.640
And 14 grams of fiber
isn't a lot.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.480
That would even take
the average U.S. diet

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.480
up to the recommended
minimum average

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.000
adequate daily fiber intake
of 38 grams for men

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.120
and 25 daily grams for women.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.960
The increased fiber intake
appeared to lead

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.720
to about a 10% drop
in daily calorie intake.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.360
Why would more fiber
mean fewer calories?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.400
Well, conventionally,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.960
fiber is considered
to have zero calories.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.080
So, it adds bulk to food
without adding extra calories,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.320
resulting in a lower
"energy-to-weight ratio"

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.840
in the food.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.520
To illustrate,
let's compare a food

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.560
to its fiber-depleted
equivalent.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.280
Consider a bottle
of cold-pressed apple juice.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.480
That's basically just an apple
with its fiber removed.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.680
You could drink a regular bottle

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.440
of juice
(about 15 ounces, 445 ml)

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.120
in a matter of seconds.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.040
But to get the same number
of calories,

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.280
you'd have to eat nearly 5 cups
(550-600 g) of apple slices.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.760
First, you'd have to chew
all those apple slices.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.240
Fiber-rich foods
require more chewing,

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.680
which slows down eating rate,

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.560
which itself can
improve satiety.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.640
That also allows
for more secretion of saliva

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.280
and stomach juices.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.800
Researchers spread
a barium paste

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:05.520
onto slices of different kinds
of bread.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.800
Talk about research
that would not

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.120
pass human safety review today,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.480
and found that on x-ray,

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.360
the stomach shadow was larger
after eating whole wheat bread

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.440
compared to white.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.120
Five grams
of a highly viscous fiber,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.800
like what's in apples and oats,

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.480
can hold approximately
a quart of water (945 ml)

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.520
as it passes through
the stomach and small intestine.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.440
So, that's having
an extra two pounds (0.9 kg)

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.560
of zero-calorie food mass
filling you up.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.400
If you feed people
the same meal,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.840
one with natural fiber

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.560
(whole wheat pasta
with pureed veggies and fruits)

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.720
and the other meal
composed of the same foods

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.640
with the fiber depleted

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.520
(white bread with fruit
and vegetable juices),

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.320
but both meals
have the same volume,

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.520
the stomach empties faster
with the fiber-depleted meal,

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.840
about 45 minutes faster.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.320
It's not what we eat,
but what we absorb.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.880
So, we can lose more weight
on a high-fiber diet

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.360
eating the exact same number
of calories,

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.280
because some of the calories
get trapped

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.920
and never make it
into our system.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.360
Those on a standard
American diet

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.560
lose about 5% of the calories
they eat in their waste.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.960
A higher-fiber diet
can double that.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.160
It's not just that the calories

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.200
in high-fiber foods
are less available to absorb.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.120
They trap calories
across the board.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.520
Feed people whole meal bread
versus white bread,

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:20.960
and stool analyses find

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.880
that we flush more calories
on the whole meal bread.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.720
Eat a Twinkie
on a high-fiber diet

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.360
and absorb
fewer Twinkie calories.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.280
It's like every
calorie label you read

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.640
gets instantly discounted
on a high-fiber diet.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.040
Most nutrition classes
will teach

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.200
that a gram of protein
has four calories,

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:44.000
a gram of fat has nine calories,
and a gram of carbs has four.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.280
But that's only on a typical
low-fiber diet.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.920
On a higher-fiber diet,
up around the average

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.240
of those eating
strictly plant-based diets,

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:55.840
the effective calorie counts
per gram drop from 4, 9, 4,

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.640
for protein, fat,
and carbs, respectively,

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:02.640
to around 3.5, 8.7, 3.8.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.880
That may not seem like a lot,

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.480
but if Americans just reached

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.720
the minimum recommended
fiber intake,

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.480
that might decrease
calorie absorption

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.200
by more than 100 calories a day.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.480
That may be enough to prevent

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.640
that average gradual
annual weight gain

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.520
most experience
through middle age.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.080
Even a small change
in daily calorie absorption

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.840
could have
long-term significance

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.899
for weight management.

